\fs18 \cf4 \cb31 \strokec4 She awakens to a pale, desolate world\cb1 \
\cb31 A hundred years is a dream too long. Long enough for the mists to swallow the remnants of a bygone age. Long enough for pale silence to smother the lingering warmth in her memory.\cb1 \
\cb31 A hundred years is a dream too short. Short enough that the smile before parting still reflects in her eyes. Short enough that her fingertips still reach for a fleeting dance.\cb1 \
\cb31 Then she remembers a summer night. The star-filled sky they once gazed upon together. So she begins to dance alone, just as she always has.\cb1 \
\cb31 Turn. Pause. Reach. Fall into empty air.\cb1 \
\cb31 To an old friend. To a bygone age.\cb1 \
\cb31 May this lament serve as the farewell that has waited a hundred years to be spoken.\cb1 \
\cb31 "Hey... Care to share a dance with me?"\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

