\fs18 \cf4 \cb31 \strokec4 Dusk spills over the rooftops of the world, and lights flicker on one by one. Behind every window glows the warmth of home.\cb1 \
\cb31 Her thin clothes do little to keep out the wind and rain. The girl once called a hero fusses over her disheveled wings.\cb1 \
\cb31 She drains a cup brimming with forgetfulness, yet searing memories still burn her throat as moonlight flows across her lowered gaze.\cb1 \
\cb31 "Be careful... The ghosts of the old world just might come knocking at your window."\cb1 \
